    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#title": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "Life Reflected in Gothenburg |  Sun, May 26, 2019, 6:00 pm | Göteborgs Konserthus"
      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#image": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "https://naccnaca-eventimages.s3.amazonaws.com/20006/bondarsphere_credit-fred-cattroll-3__large.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#description": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "Canada’s National Arts Centre Orchestra finishes its 50th Anniversary European Tour, led by renowned Music Director Alexander Shelley, in Gothenburg, Sweden.\n\n-- \n\nA stunningly original live performance, Life Reflected is a celebration of youth, promise and courage revealed in the compelling and diverse portraits of four exceptional Canadian women: Alice Munro, Amanda Todd, Roberta Bondar and Rita Joe.\n\nAlexander Shelley, Music Director of Canada’s National Arts centre Orchestra, brought together four remarkable composers to collaborate with Creative Producer and Director Donna Feore and an ensemble of extraordinary performers and..."
