    "http://ogp.me/ns#description": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "Presented in partnership with the Vancouver Symphony Orchestra and ISCM 2017\n\nPanel Discussion\n\nThis groundbreaking symphonic work is a celebration of youth, promise and courage, revealed in the compelling and diverse portraits of four women: Alice Munro, Amanda Todd, Roberta Bondar, and Rita Joe. Alexander Shelley, Music Director of the NAC Orchestra, brought together four remarkable Canadian composers - Zosha Di Castri, Jocelyn Morlock, Nicole Lizée, and John Estacio - to collaborate with Creative Producer and Director, Donna Feore, and an ensemble..."
