    "http://ogp.me/ns#description": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "This free performance for local students and members of the Eskasoni community on Cape Breton Island, Nova Scotia, will be a highlight of the NAC Orchestra Canada 150 Tour.\n\nLocal singer, Kalolin Johnson, will open the performance singing We Shall Remain with full orchestra. The NAC Orchestra will then perform the triumphant and exciting final movement to Dvorjak’s “New World Symphony.” Violin-virtuoso James Ehnes will follow with the lightening-fast third movement of the Sibelius violin concerto.\n\nThe concert will culminate with I..."
