    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#image": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "https://naccnaca-eventimages.s3.amazonaws.com/11287/cattroll-228__large.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#description": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "Who do we become when we are displaced? That’s one of the questions posed in this Friday reprise of “music on a theme of exile.”\n\nI Lost My Talk, based on the poem by Mi'kmaw elder and poet Rita Joe, C.M., was commissioned for the National Arts Centre Orchestra to commemorate the 75th birthday of The Right Honourable Joe Clark, P.C., C.C., A.O.E. by his family. World premiere.\n\nSocialize with us in the NAC lobby, have a drink, listen to live jazz,..."
      }
